0 gear-train-243 (Brickwright Robot Lab validation machine, round 2)
0 Name: gear-train-243.ldr
0 Author: Brickwright
0 !LDRAW_ORG Unofficial_Model
0 // Five 8:24 stages, 1:243 (Robot Lab validation round 2, test/bw-sim-validation-2.test.mjs).
0 // Bench: the SPIKE medium motor (port A) output up at the origin (LDraw, -y up); a Technic beam 15 under the
0 // housing (centre x = 100, holes x = -40 ... 240) pinned into the housing's bottom holes u0/u1 by friction pins.
0 // Axles k = 1..5 stand in the beam's holes at x = 40k (centres 10 + 30 = 40 LDU apart, pitch radii 1.25 LDU per
0 // tooth). Stage k (k = 0..4) is one gear width (20 LDU) above the last: an 8T on axle k at y = -60 - 20k drives a
0 // 24T on axle k+1 at the same height; axle k+1 carries the next stage's 8T one layer up. Layers rise
0 // monotonically, so no 24T shares a layer with a non-meshing 8T 40 LDU away (two layers would close a
0 // second, inconsistent mesh). Output/input = (-8/24)^5 = -1/243.
